kernora-desktop (1.4.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * The installer keeps the wallet off on systems that log in
    automatically: without a password at login the wallet cannot be
    unlocked, and saving a Wi-Fi password would open KDE's wallet setup.
  * Ctrl+Alt+T opens the terminal, as it did with Konsole.
  * A terminal started as plain alacritty shows the Kernora terminal icon
    and name instead of the Wayland logo; kernora-terminal-entry updates
    the entry in existing accounts.

