kernora-desktop (1.4.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Kernora sounds: tools/gen-sound-theme synthesises the sound theme
    "kernora" when the package is built. Soft glass and mallet tones in D
    major pentatonic, lower and darker for errors, a rising chord for the
    login, short tails, levels matched; it covers every event Plasma plays,
    the speaker test channels included, and inherits freedesktop for the
    rest.
  * The theme is the default: /etc/xdg/kdeglobals, GSettings and the GTK
    settings of new accounts name it, and a kconf_update script moves
    existing accounts off Ocean once. The login chime is on
    (/etc/xdg/plasma_workspace.notifyrc).

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700

kernora-desktop (1.4.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * GTK applications in Material 3: the Kernora GTK themes (Kernora,
    KernoraMD1, KernoraMD2, tools/gen-gtk-theme) keep Breeze GTK's
    structure and the Kernora colours and give buttons, fields, check boxes,
    radio buttons, switches, sliders, menus and tooltips the Material shapes
    and roles, so their dialogs no longer look like KDE's.
  * The theme is the default: GSettings' gtk-theme and the settings.ini of
    new accounts name it, and a kconf_update script moves existing accounts
    off Breeze once, leaving any other theme a user chose.
  * LibreWolf's own dialogs in Material 3: the browser draws them itself and
    takes only colours from GTK, so tools/gen-browser-theme also writes a
    userChrome.css with tonal and filled pill buttons for them, and
    kernora.js lets LibreWolf load it. A kconf_update script links it into
    the account's LibreWolf profiles once, leaving a user's own
    userChrome.css alone, and prepares the profile of a new account, so the
    first start has it too.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0700

kernora-desktop (1.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Install the Material 3 components as QML modules for the Kernora
    applications: org.kernora.m3 (tokens, text, icons, sliders, state
    layers) and org.kernora.ui (list rows, groups, pages, dialogs, fields,
    search, navigation, snackbars).
  * Light variants of the Plasma theme and the window decoration, so light
    or dark switches the whole system; both palettes in the QML tokens.
  * Material text is drawn with Qt's own rendering: native rendering
    spaced glyphs unevenly under Material's letter spacing.
  * App icons for the Kernora applications, the Terminal and the
    installer, drawn like the Settings icon; new Material Symbols for the
    applications.
  * Terminal: Alacritty under the Kernora name, with light and dark colours
    from the design tokens, as the desktop's terminal; its window is titled
    after the prompt ("user@host: ~") rather than "Alacritty".
  * KDE's System Settings, Alacritty and Calamares entries are hidden in
    favour of the Kernora ones.
  * Default account picture: the mark on a tonal circle.
  * Kernora login screen for SDDM: Kernora Shapes behind a large clock and
    a Material 3 account card, in English and Russian.
  * Installer: Material 3 steps, buttons and pages (welcome, location,
    keyboard, account, summary, finish), a slideshow over Kernora Shapes,
    and the kernora-installer launcher, which starts Calamares with the
    Kernora look in the session's language.
  * Installer keyboard: a Material 3 keyboard that shows what every key
    types in the chosen layout and variant (from XKB, by
    tools/gen-keyboard-maps) and lights up while typing; layout, variant,
    model and switch as dropdown fields, named in the installer's language
    (xkeyboard-config's translations), also on the summary.
  * Installer: cities sorted by their translated names; Russian for the
    messages Calamares leaves untranslated (tools/gen-qm); the live
    language service is removed from the installed system.
  * Installer partition page in Material 3 with Kernora's Calamares: option
    cards, partition list and dialogs styled by the branding's stylesheet.qss
    (tools/gen-installer-style), Material Symbols for its icons
    (tools/gen-installer-icons); kernora-calamares depends on calamares
    (>= 3.3.14-1kernora1).
  * Push buttons without icons (ShowIconsOnPushButtons=false), as Material
    buttons carry text only.
  * Kernora lock screen: Kernora Shapes behind a large clock, the account
    card with its password pill and the power actions, as on the login
    screen. It replaces Plasma's (diverted) and unlocks through the same
    kscreenlocker authenticator.
  * Kernora on-screen display: volume and brightness as a thick Material 3
    slider with the icon riding on the fill, messages as a pill; replaces
    Plasma's (diverted).
  * Kernora power menu for log out, restart and shut down: large Material 3
    tiles on a card, the automatic action counting down.
  * Alt+Tab shows Kernora window cards (a KWin window switcher): the app's
    icon and title over a rounded thumbnail, the chosen card ringed.
  * The web browser is LibreWolf, in the Kernora colours: a generated light
    and dark theme (tools/gen-browser-theme) that LibreWolf installs into
    new profiles as a distribution add-on, made the default by kernora.js
    in /usr/share/librewolf/browser/defaults/preferences (read after the
    browser's own defaults), which also has files picked in Kernora's
    chooser through the desktop portal. LibreWolf's own policies (uBlock
    Origin, no telemetry) are left as they are.
  * /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list: LibreWolf opens web pages and PDFs, Photos
    pictures, the Text Editor JSON and XML (LibreWolf claims those too).
  * Kernora notifications: popups laid out like Android's (the app's
    badge, "App · time", title, text, the picture beside it, tonal action
    buttons, M3 progress for file jobs) and a history of connected cards
    with Do not disturb and "Clear all"; the panel bell badges unread
    notifications and rings with the jobs' progress. Plasma's applet keeps
    its C++ plugin; its QML entry point is diverted.
  * Notification job details show how much is copied again (Plasma's
    QML failed on an undeclared variable).
  * Quick settings: Android's media card for whatever plays (any MPRIS
    player) -- the artwork behind a scrim, a play button that squares off
    while playing, and a seek bar that flows as a wave.
  * Quick settings: a Dark Theme tile, which switches the whole system the
    way Settings does (org.kernora.system's Appearance), and a Screenshot
    tile, which starts the Screenshot app once the shade is gone. On a
    short screen (a 768px laptop, the media card showing) the shade's
    content scrolls inside it instead of running past its edge; the handle
    strip at the top still closes it with a swipe.
  * Lock screen: the playing media's controls at the bottom centre, usable
    without unlocking.
  * Push buttons carry their text alone, in QML (the Kernora Qt Quick
    Controls style) and in widget dialogs (Kvantum's iconless_pushbutton)
    alike; icon-only buttons keep their icon.
  * Task manager: application counts as Material badges (error-coloured
    pills), and window previews and album art in the tooltips on rounded
    tiles without drop shadows (Badge.qml and ToolTipInstance.qml
    diverted).
  * Alt+Space opens the Kernora launcher and its search; KRunner's own
    window keeps Alt+F2 (its kglobalaccel service file is diverted).
  * Kernora boot splash (tools/gen-plymouth-theme): the mark on the dark
    surface and Material 3's loading indicator, the expressive shapes
    turning into one another; a passphrase prompt in a pill. Plymouth's
    defaults are diverted to it, and /etc/default/grub.d/kernora.cfg adds
    "splash" to the installed system's kernel command line.
  * The splash hands over to the login screen without a text console in
    between: Plymouth quits keeping its last frame (a plymouth-quit.service
    drop-in), and the console cursor is off.
  * Kernora boot menu (tools/gen-grub-theme): the mark over the entries as
    rounded Material cards, the chosen one on the secondary container, in
    Roboto (GRUB fonts made at build time with grub-mkfont, Cyrillic
    included). The ISO carries it, and grub.d/kernora.cfg sets it with the
    graphical terminal for an installed system.
  * Styles: Material Design 1, 2 and 3. tools/kernora_design.py defines all
    three generations from the one seed, and the QML tokens carry them all,
    following ~/.config/kernorarc at run time:
    - their palettes: grey paper with a vivid accent; white and #121212;
      tonal;
    - their corners per kind of component, and their shadows;
    - their buttons: capitals and raised in the older two, pills in
      Material 3;
    - their switches, sliders and quick settings: Lollipop's bare icons,
      Android 9's round toggles, Material 3's tiles.
    The colour schemes, Plasma theme, Kvantum and window frames are
    generated for each (KernoraMD2Dark, kernora-md2, ...). The shell, the
    Qt Quick style and the shared components follow, with Material 3's own
    expressive details kept.
  * Kernora clipboard (org.kernora.clipboard): Meta+V opens the clipboard
    history as a Material 3 sheet above the panel, with search, text,
    links, pictures and files as connected cards, "Remove" and "Clear
    all". It loads Plasma's Klipper, which nothing in the panel started
    before; Klipper's own popup leaves Meta+V to it (a kglobalshortcutsrc
    for new accounts), and the history keeps pictures (/etc/xdg/klipperrc).
  * The sheet's second tab is emoji, as on a phone keyboard: Meta+. opens
    it (Plasma's emoji selector's shortcut file is diverted), with
    category tabs, recently used ones, search by English and Russian names
    and keywords, and Noto Color Emoji. The emoji and their names are
    generated from Unicode's and CLDR's data (tools/gen-emoji-data).
  * A USB drive or memory card plugged in brings a notification from Files
    ("USB drive connected", with "Open"), which mounts it and opens it in
    Files; Kernora's panel has no device notifier to pop up instead
    (quick settings' DeviceSource.qml on Plasma's device model,
    kernora-devices.notifyrc).
  * Plasma theme: the focus and hover rings of fields and buttons sit on the
    control (Plasma lays them out by their margins, which drew KRunner's
    focus ring 16px around its field), and pill fields and buttons are half
    as round as they are tall, so no seam runs through their middle.
  * Material Symbols for the OSD's switches (Wi-Fi, touchpad, on-screen
    keyboard, mobile data, sleep blocked), for the display switch (Meta+P:
    one screen, the other, mirrored, extended left or right), and for
    reply, send and clear; links as Material's link symbol.
  * Login screen without SDDM's on-screen keyboard, which covered the
    account card.
  * New panels and launchers pin Files and Settings instead of KDE's
    System Settings.
  * The settings window of the desktop and of every applet in Kernora's
    layout: sections as a navigation list, the current one on a rounded
    pane under its headline, Material buttons. The desktop's pages are
    Material groups -- wallpaper and desktop kind as choices, the folder
    view's Location, Icons and Filter, Mouse Actions with a dialog that
    catches the new click, an applet's shortcut, and About. Plasma's files
    are diverted; what they save is unchanged. Buttons at the end of a
    list row take their own clicks (they went to the row). Plasma's
    picture and slideshow pages get room for their grid of pictures.
  * Material Symbols: create_new_folder for folder-new.
  * Live wallpapers of Material shapes at play, next to Kernora Shapes and
    in its flat Material 3 tones: Tower (a stack of shapes rocks, tumbles
    down and hops back together, simulated on the shapes' outlines),
    Rhythm (a ring of shapes in a pendulum wave -- spirals, stars and back
    to a circle -- over a blob that morphs with it) and Marble Run (shape
    marbles roll down ramps, ring the posts and ride a lift back up); each
    with a tonal palette from gen-wallpaper-assets, which also gives the
    shapes' convex hulls. Picture
    wallpapers are gone: Kernora Ember is removed and Breeze's picture is
    kept out by a dpkg path-exclude.
  * Kernora cursors (kernora_cursors, tools/gen-cursor-theme): Material
    glyphs with ember badges; wait and progress animate Material 3
    Expressive's morphing loading indicator. Xcursor and KWin's scalable
    SVGs; the default in Plasma, SDDM and x-cursor-theme.
  * No bouncing icon while programs start (/etc/xdg/klaunchrc): the busy
    cursor is the only launch feedback.
  * org.kernora.ui: StyleCard removed; the style is chosen from a list.

